-This strategy first computes a vector embedding for the new candidate concept, then computes cosine similarity between this embedding and the pre-computed embeddings of every existing node in the graph. Only nodes whose similarity strictly exceeds a fixed threshold are shortlisted for the final LLM decision step. Following the precedent established in \[2\], the threshold is fixed at 0.6 before any experimental run and is not tuned on this study's own evaluation data; this keeps the shortlist rule from being adjusted after seeing results. To show how sensitive the findings are to this choice, the threshold is additionally evaluated at 0.4 and 0.5 as separate sensitivity runs (Section 3.4). Similarity is computed as cosine similarity between embeddings produced by the all-MiniLM-L6-v2 sentence-embedding model run locally on CPU, and the shortlist may be empty, in which case no LLM call is made for that insertion.
